<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seretse Khama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seretse Khama was the hereditary chief of the Bangwato and the first President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, from 1966 until his death in 1980. His marriage to an Englishwoman, Ruth Williams, led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to exile him from the Bechuanaland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> in the 1950s. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana-democratic-party">Botswana Democratic Party</a> and led the country to independence and stable democratic government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seretse-khama.jpg" alt="Seretse Khama" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Communities Director: Allan Watson Architect: Jean Polak,Jean Gilson,Lucien De Vestel,André Polak · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seretse_Khama_1977_(2).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
